    "https://www.eur.nl/en/working-at-eur/vacancies/policy-coordinator-educational-quality-innovation": {
      "title": "Policy Coordinator, Educational Quality & Innovation",
      "description": "Policy Coordinator, Educational Quality & Innovation | Working at | Erasmus University Rotterdam Skip to main content Skip to search Skip to subnavigation Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Close Open search Close Open menu Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Switch language to EN English current language NL Nederlands Search Close Search Search Primary Why work at EUR Open submenu Why work at EUR Campus Diversity Societal involvement Sustainability Working conditions Working areas Open submenu Working areas Academic staff Working in Finance Working in IT Working at Legal Affairs Working at Real Estate & Facilities PhD LDE traineeship International staff Practical information Open submenu Practical information Candidate portal Vacancies Policy Coordinator, Educational Quality & Innovation Listen Published Friday 16 Oct 2026 Deadline Friday 30 Oct 2026 Work area Education Organisational unit Rotterdam School of Management (RSM) Salary € 3.706 - € 5.760 Employment 0.9 fte - 1 fte Introduction As policy coordinator at Rotterdam School of Management, Erasmus University (RSM) , the largest faculty at Erasmus University Rotterdam , you coordinate the policy field of continuous improvement in RSM’s education as your primary dossier. You are RSM’s point of reference for how continuous improvement is designed, embedded, governed and evidenced across our pre-experience programme portfolio. We have deliberately built the requirements of our external accreditations into our own continuous improvement policy rather than running them as a parallel exercise. Your work therefore serves two simultaneous purposes: it strengthens the quality of our programmes; and it keeps RSM continuously accreditation-ready. Continuous improvement is your primary dossier. Alongside it, you hold a small number of longer-term policy dossiers within the Quality & Innovation portfolio and you take on other policy assignments on an ad-hoc basis. You report to the Executive Director Quality and Innovation and work closely with colleagues responsible for or contributing to the quality and innovation portfolio, with academic directors and programme teams and with portfolio- and school-level committees. Our business school is a dynamic and strongly internationally oriented organisation. In total there are about 650 employees, the majority of whom work in the academic departments. We have a public entity (RSM EUR), and a private entity (RSM BV) where, for example, we offer our MBA programmes. Your work focuses on the public entity. Job description Your position carries a defined mandate: You are the custodian of the RSM continuous improvement maturity model , formally adopted at the school level and you determine and report where each programme stands against it. You have a standing reporting line into senior management through the Executive Director Quality and Innovation, including a defined escalation route where programmes do not reach the minimally required maturity level. You guide and support, but do not direct , programme stakeholders. Your effectiveness rests on evidence, professional authority and organisational sensitivity rather than on hierarchical position. Your responsibilities fall into four areas. Continuous improvement policy and frameworks Under the direction of the Executive Director Quality & Innovation, you develop and maintain the policies, frameworks and standards that define continuous improvement at RSM and keep them aligned with evolving accreditation requirements. Monitoring and reporting You coordinate RSM’s continuous improvement cycle across programme, portfolio and school levels. You monitor and report on programme maturity and progress of improvement actions to inform senior management and supply the evidence needed for accreditation and external reviews. Guidance and implementation You guide academic directors and programme teams in meeting and moving beyond RSM’s continuous improvement standards and lead improvement initiatives at different levels. Other policy dossiers and assignments You hold a small number of policy topics as longer-term dossiers. You stay informed of developments so that you can act quickly when action is needed. Other topics are assigned ad-hoc, as developments such as new regulation, university- or school-wide policy initiatives or questions from within the school call for them. The dossiers and assignments you cover may change in line with the priorities of the school and the Q&I portfolio. In both cases, you analyse the implications for RSM, coordinate stakeholder consultations and prepare policy proposals. You proactively liaise with those responsible for the areas concerned and for the school’s policy processes so that your proposals are actionable and pragmatic. Your challenges can include: Securing genuine policy adoption across programmes that differ substantially in maturity, capacity, and appetite – without hierarchical authority. Enforcing agreed standards and deadlines with busy senior academic and professional colleagues, sensitively and effectively. Coming to grips quickly with policy topics and turning them, often at short notice, into proposals that are both well-founded and workable for the school. Balancing the fixed annual rhythm of continuous improvement with other policy work that may arrive unannounced. Job requirements You read organisations well and win over senior colleagues with evidence and argument, not authority. You turn abstract quality or policy principles into frameworks people actually understand and use and you distil a clear portfolio picture from what is happening across programmes. You set your own priorities, keeping the annual cycle on track while staying ready for the policy questions no one saw coming. And you write with precision and clarity: documents that get adopted and then get used. Job requirements An academic degree at the master level At least three years of relevant experience in quality assurance, educational policy or continuous improvement, preferably in higher education Demonstrable experience in drafting policy documents, frameworks or governance instruments that have been formally adopted and used Demonstrable experience in advising and influencing senior stakeholders without hierarchical authority Strong knowledge of accreditation and quality assurance in higher education; experience with assurance of learning is an advantage Experience in leading cross-functional initiatives Confident and critical use of AI tools for analysis and reporting, including the judgement to verify what they produce before acting on it Proficiency in English at C1 CEFR level. Dutch at B2 CEFR level or higher preferred. Employment conditions and benefits We offer you an internationally oriented and varied job in an enthusiastic team, with excellent working conditions in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities (CAO-NU) . The start date of this position will be determined by mutual agreement and you will be based at the Quality & Innovation Department in Rotterdam School of Management, Erasmus University (RSM). This position is for 0.9 FTE - FTE. The salary is dependent on your experience and knowledge and ranges from a minimum of € 3,706 to a maximum of € 5,760 gross per month Scale 10 on a fulltime basis (38 hours), in accordance with the CAO-NU. If you are selected, you will be offered a contract for a period of one (1) year which can be converted into an employment contract for an indefinite period if suitability is proven and if you continue in the same position, and if (financial and/or organisational) circumstances remain the same. Read below to see everything else we have to offer you! - Everything you need for a good work-life balance : the option to work from home in consultation with your manager, 41 days of paid leave with a 40 hour contract, 8% holiday pay and an 8.3% end-of-year bonus, and a significant discount on a subscription for our on-campus sports centre ! - Sustainable, inclusive and diverse work environment with an open culture, where you can be yourself and we pay attention to each other and to the world around us. Make the most of our bicycle budget, or join networks such as Young@EUR , FAME , EUR Disability Staff Network or QuEUR. - Time and space for your development in the broadest sense: development days and a personal career budget and free access to our university library . - Good pension with ABP that EUR contributes two-thirds towards, discounts on various collective insurances with Zilveren Kruis Achmea, Loyalis, and Allianz, and compensation for travel, working from home and home internet use. - Are you currently combining your job with parenthood, or do you want to do so in the future? EUR offers partially paid parental leave and fully paid additional birth leave for partners , and our campus features a daycare (daycare not paid for by EUR). - Moving to the Netherlands for your job with EUR? Then you may be eligible for the Expat-ruling if you meet the requirements of the Belastingdienst (Dutch tax agency), and with our Dual Career Programme we will also help your partner find the right job for them. Employer Erasmus University Rotterdam (EUR) is an internationally oriented university with a strong social orientation in its education and research, as expressed in our mission ‘Creating positive societal impact’. EUR is home to 4.100 academics and professionals and almost 33.000 students from more than 140 countries. Everything we do, we do under the credo The Erasmian Way – Making Minds Matter. We’re global citizens, connecting, entrepreneurial, open-minded, and socially involved. These Erasmian Values function as our internal compass and create EUR’s distinctive and recognizable profile. From these values, with a broad perspective and with an eye for diversity, different backgrounds and opinions, our employees work closely together to solve societal challenges from the dynamic and cosmopolitan city of Rotterdam. Thanks to the high quality and positive societal impact of our research and education, EUR can compete with the top European universities. www.eur.nl . Faculty / Institute / Central service Rotterdam School of Management, Erasmus University (RSM) is one of Europe’s top-ranked business schools. RSM provides ground-breaking research and education furthering excellence in all aspects of management and is based in the international port city of Rotterdam – a vital nexus of business, logistics and trade. RSM’s primary focus is on developing business leaders with international careers who can become a force for positive change by carrying their innovative mindset into a sustainable future. Our first-class range of bachelor, master, MBA, PhD and executive programmes encourage them to become critical, creative, caring and collaborative thinkers and doers. www.rsm.nl RSM is an equal opportunity employer and explicitly encourages applications from candidates of all genders, ethnicities, and nationalities. Applying To apply for this vacancy, please submit your application before Friday 30 October, by applying via the portal. Be sure to include both your CV and motivational letter. Have any questions, need additional information or would you like to discuss your candidacy? Please reach out to Anna de Waard-Leung at leung2@rsm.nl . We look forward to receiving your application! Please note: If a candidate is found to be suitable, we may invite them for an interview even before the closing date. Stay up to date with new vacancies! Want to be the first to know about vacancies that match your interests? Let us know what you're looking for, and we'll send you an email as soon as a new opportunity that fits your profile is posted.\nDon’t miss out on your perfect job! Sign up Close Stay up to date with new vacancies! Share this page Interested? Applicant portal Open navigation for Policy Coordinator, Educational Quality & Innovation Close Interested? Interested? Compare @count study programme Close Compare @count study programme @title Duration: @duration Remove @title Compare study programmes Breadcrumb Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Vacancies Policy Coordinator, Educational Quality & Innovation Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Directly to Information Directly to Why work at EUR Working areas International staff Practical information Vacancies Information ANBI Cookies Disclaimer Privacy statement Accessibility Our channels Facebook Instagram X (formerly twitter) Linkedin Youtube Making Minds Matter Watch the video Close"
    },
    "https://www.eur.nl/en/working-at-eur/vacancies/projectcontroller-0": {
      "title": "Projectcontroller",
      "description": "Projectcontroller | Working at | Erasmus University Rotterdam Skip to main content Skip to search Skip to subnavigation Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Close Open search Close Open menu Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Switch language to EN English current language NL Nederlands Search Close Search Search Featured results Primary Why work at EUR Open submenu Why work at EUR Campus Diversity Societal involvement Sustainability Working conditions Working areas Open submenu Working areas Academic staff Working in Finance Working in IT Working at Legal Affairs Working at Real Estate & Facilities PhD LDE traineeship International staff Practical information Open submenu Practical information Candidate portal Vacancies Projectcontroller Listen This vacancy is only available in Dutch. Use the button below to view it in Dutch. View vacancy in Dutch Open navigation for Projectcontroller Close Compare 0 study programmes Close Compare 0 study programmes 0 of 3 study programmes selected. @title Duration: @duration Remove @title Compare study programmes Breadcrumb Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Vacancies Projectcontroller Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Directly to Information Directly to Why work at EUR Working areas International staff Practical information Vacancies Information ANBI Cookies Disclaimer Privacy statement Accessibility Our channels Facebook Instagram X (formerly twitter) Linkedin Youtube Making Minds Matter Watch the video Close Our website uses cookies Overview This website uses cookies and similar technologies (hereinafter collectively: 'cookies'). In this menu, you can choose which types of cookies and purposes you consent to. Functional: ​​These cookies are technically necessary for the website to function properly. Using the website is not possible without accepting these cookies. Analytics: These cookies are used to analyze and improve website usage in general. We take measures to ensure that your privacy is not, or only minimally, affected by these cookies. It's highly appreciated if you toggle the switch. Marketing & Social Media: If you want marketing campaigns and advertisements you see online and on social media to be tailored to your browsing behavior and the interests derived from it, you can enable the slider or click the 'Accept all' button. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time by making new choices in the menu. Click on 'Overview' at the top for a complete overview of the cookies in each category. Please see our cookies page for more information and to reset your cookie preferences. Functional Analytics Marketing & Social Media Reject all Accept Selection Accept all Eur.nl Functional Cookies and similar technologies that are strictly necessary for the website to work, such as remembering your preferences, security, enabling log-in or processing forms. Consent Studio Consent Studio consent-studio__consent-id ID of the proof of consent storage within the Consent Studio platform. 30 days consent-studio__storage Local storage for the consent given by the user for certain categories of cookies. 30 days consent-studio__seen Boolean that keeps track of whether the user has seen the cookie banner at least once. 30 days consent-studio__implicit-consent-triggered When a website has implicit consent configured, this cookie stores whether or not it has been triggered or not. 30 days consent-studio__gpc-consent-triggered Records that your browser's Global Privacy Control signal was detected, so non-essential cookies were automatically declined on your behalf. 30 days Cloudflare Cloudflare __cf_bm Helps Cloudflare tell people and automated programs apart, to protect the site from bots. 30 minutes _cfuvid Lets Cloudflare tell apart visitors who share the same internet connection, so traffic limits are applied fairly. Session cf_clearance Remembers that you passed a Cloudflare security check, so you are not asked again. 30 minutes HubSpot HubSpot hs_sessionid* Identifies your current visit so HubSpot can keep your session consistent while you browse. — Erasmus University Rotterdam CMS personalisation.segments This collects anonymous data about which category a visitor fits into. This allows us to offer the visitor content that matches their profile, based on visiting behaviour. — OnlineAfspraken.nl OnlineAfspraken.nl booking widget oa-dao-Resource* Stores the list of bookable resources, such as staff or rooms, that the appointment widget can offer. — oa-dao-ConsumerForm* Stores the layout and field definitions of the booking form, not the details you enter. — oa-dao-AppTypeGroup* Stores the categories used to group appointment types in the booking widget. — oa-booking Stores the details of the appointment you are currently booking. — oa-dao-* Stores appointment widget reference data on your device so the booking form does not have to reload it on every visit. — oa-application-widget-booking-consumerwidget-state Stores technical state the booking widget needs to work. — oa-dao-Mailing-MailingList-* Stores a mailing list that the appointment widget can offer you to subscribe to. — oa-configHash Stores a code used to check whether the booking widget has changed, so out-of-date saved booking data can be cleared. — oa-consumer Stores the identity of the signed-in customer for the booking. — oa-dao-AppType* Stores the list of appointment types the booking widget can offer. — oa-shoppingcart Stores the items you have added to your booking basket. — Analytics These cookies and similar technologies collect information about how visitors use our website, such as which pages are visited most, whether errors occur, and how users interact, to help us measure performance and improve the site. Google Google Analytics _ga ID used to identify users 2 years _ga_* Keeps track of your current visit for one specific Google Analytics property. 2 years eur.nl Website FPID Registers statistical data on users' behaviour on the website. Used for internal analytics by the website operator. — FPLC This FPLC cookie is the cross-domain linker cookie hashed from the FPID cookie. It’s not HttpOnly, which means it can be read with JavaScript. It has a relatively short lifetime, just 20 hours. — *__ga_* Keeps track of your current visit for one specific Google Analytics property. — *__ga Identifies your browser so Google Analytics can tell returning visitors from new ones. — *_FPID Identifies returning visitors so Google Analytics can report on visit patterns over time. 2 years *_FPLC Helps Google Analytics keep a consistent visitor identifier when you move between this site's subdomains or linked domains. 20 hours Hotjar Hotjar _hjSessionUser_* Stores a random ID that lets Hotjar recognise you when you return to the site. 1 year _hjSession_* Links the pages you view during one visit to the same Hotjar session. 30 minutes Marketing & Social Media These cookies and similar technologies help advertising and social media partners personalise your experience, show you relevant ads, measure campaign results, and enable sharing features. Google Google Ads _gcl_au Identifies your browser so Google can link a later purchase or sign-up on this site to the adverts you saw or clicked. 90 days IDE Recognises your browser so Google can measure how adverts perform and show you adverts that fit your interests. 13 months _gcl_ls This item is used by Google Ads to store advertising click identifiers for conversion measurement. When visitors do not accept tracking cookies, Google can send a cookieless ping via Consent Mode v2 with anonymized data to measure conversions and advertising performance. Data may be stored temporarily or persistently, depending on the implementation. — Google NID Lets Google remember your preferences and helps it choose which adverts to show you. 6 months __Secure-ENID Remembers your Google preferences, such as language, and can be used to choose which adverts you see. 13 months eur.nl Website FPAU Identifies your browser so Google can link a later purchase or sign-up on this site to the adverts you saw or clicked. 90 days *__fbp Stores a Meta (Facebook) browser identifier so visits and conversions can be attributed back to Meta advertising. — *__gcl_au Identifies your browser so Google can link a later purchase or sign-up on this site to the adverts you saw or clicked. 90 days *_FPAU Identifies your browser so Google can link a later purchase or sign-up on this site to the adverts you saw or clicked. 90 days LinkedIn LinkedIn lidc Helps LinkedIn choose which of its data centres handles your browser's requests. 1 day bcookie Identifies your browser to LinkedIn when LinkedIn content or advertising is loaded on this site. 1 year li_gc Remembers whether you agreed to LinkedIn's non-essential cookies as a visitor without a LinkedIn account. 6 months Meta Meta Pixel _fbp Identifies your browser to Meta, so your visits to this site can be used for advertising on Facebook and Instagram and to measure how adverts perform. 90 days lastExternalReferrer Detects how the user reached the website by registering their last URL-address — lastExternalReferrerTime Detects how the user reached the website by registering their last URL-address — Consent dialog opened"
    },
