    "https://www.eur.nl/en/working-at-eur/vacancies/tutor-academy-ta-technology-strategy-20262027": {
      "title": "Tutor Academy TA Technology Strategy 2026/2027",
      "description": "Tutor Academy TA Technology Strategy 2026/2027 | Working at | Erasmus University Rotterdam Skip to main content Skip to search Skip to subnavigation Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Close Open search Close Open menu Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Switch language to EN English current language NL Nederlands Search Close Search Search Featured results Primary Why work at EUR Open submenu Why work at EUR Campus Diversity Societal involvement Sustainability Working conditions Working areas Open submenu Working areas Academic staff Working in Finance Working in IT Working at Legal Affairs Working at Real Estate & Facilities PhD LDE traineeship International staff Practical information Open submenu Practical information Candidate portal Vacancies Tutor Academy TA Technology Strategy 2026/2027 Listen Published Sunday 25 Oct 2026 Deadline Friday 6 Nov 2026 Work area Education Organisational unit Rotterdam School of Management (RSM) Salary € 3.230 - € 3.288 Employment 0.1 fte - 0.4 fte Introduction Firms need to innovate to stay competitive. Kodak and Nokia are amongst the many examples of companies that paid the price for not keeping up with the market. However, innovation is difficult and while successful innovations promise large returns, many projects fail. This has never been more accurate than in the Digital Age, as fast-paced and complex technologies such as AI now permeate businesses and products. Job description As a TA you will help with the grading of case reports that discuss the transformative impact of digital technologies on businesses and economies. You have the chance to dive deep into the opportunities and challenges of the Digital Revolution and you can practice your own case skills. You will work for a total of 50h between Dec 2026 and Feb 2027. The case report is assessed during exam (Dec 14 for the exam and Feb 8 for the resit), so you will mostly need to work on the grading after exams, i.e., mid-late Dec and early-mid Feb. There is some flexibility in the allocation of hours. Job requirements Applicants must be registered in the Netherlands. Applicants must have a Dutch address, a Dutch social security number (“BSN”), and a work permit. Applicants must have completed their Bachelor's degree. Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at the Erasmus university. The ideal candidate has attained very good results in previous case-based classes, is a strong writer, and has a very good command of the English language. A background in innovation, technology management, strategy, or economics is a plus. Employment conditions and benefits You will be paid in accordance with the standard university TA contract (around €19 gross hourly rate for Master’s students). Please keep in mind that the salary rate may differ slightly based on the contract that you will receive for the specific vacancy. You will also receive a free didactical training that takes about a day. There will be no monetary compensation for this training, but we aim to provide a high-quality training that, upon completion, can be meaningfully listed on your CV. Employer Erasmus University Rotterdam (EUR) is an internationally oriented university with a strong social orientation in its education and research, as expressed in our mission ‘Creating positive societal impact’. EUR is home to 4.100 academics and professionals and almost 33.000 students from more than 140 countries. Everything we do, we do under the credo The Erasmian Way – Making Minds Matter. We’re global citizens, connecting, entrepreneurial, open-minded, and socially involved. These Erasmian Values function as our internal compass and create EUR’s distinctive and recognizable profile. From these values, with a broad perspective and with an eye for diversity, different backgrounds and opinions, our employees work closely together to solve societal challenges from the dynamic and cosmopolitan city of Rotterdam. Thanks to the high quality and positive societal impact of our research and education, EUR can compete with the top European universities. www.eur.nl . Faculty / Institute / Central service Rotterdam School of Management, Erasmus University (RSM) is one of Europe’s top-ranked business schools. RSM provides ground-breaking research and education furthering excellence in all aspects of management and is based in the international port city of Rotterdam – a vital nexus of business, logistics and trade. RSM’s primary focus is on developing business leaders with international careers who can become a force for positive change by carrying their innovative mindset into a sustainable future. Our first-class range of bachelor, master, MBA, PhD and executive programmes encourage them to become critical, creative, caring and collaborative thinkers and doers. RSM is an equal opportunity employer and explicitly encourages applications from candidates of all genders, ethnicities, and nationalities. www.rsm.nl Opens external Applying Please submit your CV, full transcripts of records of all completed university degrees, and a brief motivation the Tutor Academy recruitment platform. If you have previously worked as a TA for the Erasmus University Rotterdam, please include your previous contract start and end dates. Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis. Early application is strongly encouraged. If you have any questions, please do not hesitate to reach out to j.tang@rsm.nl or tutoracademy@rsm.nl Stay up to date with new vacancies! Want to be the first to know about vacancies that match your interests? Let us know what you're looking for, and we'll send you an email as soon as a new opportunity that fits your profile is posted.\nDon’t miss out on your perfect job! Sign up Close Stay up to date with new vacancies! Job alert Please select your preferences. When a new job becomes available that matches these preference we'll send you an email. Fields marked with a * are required. First Name Last Name Email address Password Your password requires a minimum of 8 characters of which 2 non-alphabetic Confirm password Business Unit Any Erasmus School of Economics (ESE) Erasmus School of Law (ESL) Erasmus School of History, Culture and Communication (ESHCC) Erasmus School of Social and Behavioural Sciences (ESSB) Erasmus School of Philosophy (ESPhil) Rotterdam School of Management (RSM) International Institute of Social Studies (ISS) Erasmus School of Health Policy & Management (ESHPM) General Management Directorate (ABD) University Library (UB) Convergence Human Resources (HR) Finance (FIN) Education and Student Affairs (E&S) Erasmus Digitalisation and Information Services (EDIS) Real Estate & Facilities (RE&F) Engagement & Research Services (ERS) Marketing & Communications (M&C) RSM BV Institute for Housing and Urban Development Studies (IHS) Any Any Erasmus School of Economics (ESE) Erasmus School of Law (ESL) Erasmus School of History, Culture and Communication (ESHCC) Erasmus School of Social and Behavioural Sciences (ESSB) Erasmus School of Philosophy (ESPhil) Rotterdam School of Management (RSM) International Institute of Social Studies (ISS) Erasmus School of Health Policy & Management (ESHPM) General Management Directorate (ABD) University Library (UB) Convergence Human Resources (HR) Finance (FIN) Education and Student Affairs (E&S) Erasmus Digitalisation and Information Services (EDIS) Real Estate & Facilities (RE&F) Engagement & Research Services (ERS) Marketing & Communications (M&C) RSM BV Institute for Housing and Urban Development Studies (IHS) OK Cancel Expertise Any Administration & Secretariat Policy & Advice IT Marketing & Communication Human Resources Finance Legal Real Estate & Facilities Management Education Research, development, innovation Academic staff PhD Procurement Any Any Administration & Secretariat Policy & Advice IT Marketing & Communication Human Resources Finance Legal Real Estate & Facilities Management Education Research, development, innovation Academic staff PhD Procurement OK Cancel Share this page Interested? Apply now Applicant portal Open navigation for Tutor Academy TA Technology Strategy 2026/2027 Close Interested? Apply now Interested? Apply now Compare 0 study programmes Close Compare 0 study programmes 0 of 3 study programmes selected. @title Duration: @duration Remove @title Compare study programmes Breadcrumb Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Vacancies Tutor Academy TA Technology Strategy 2026/2027 Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Directly to Information Directly to Why work at EUR Working areas International staff Practical information Vacancies Information ANBI Cookies Disclaimer Privacy statement Accessibility Our channels Facebook Instagram X (formerly twitter) Linkedin Youtube Making Minds Matter Watch the video Close Our website uses cookies Overview This website uses cookies and similar technologies (hereinafter collectively: 'cookies'). In this menu, you can choose which types of cookies and purposes you consent to. Functional: ​​These cookies are technically necessary for the website to function properly. Using the website is not possible without accepting these cookies. Analytics: These cookies are used to analyze and improve website usage in general. We take measures to ensure that your privacy is not, or only minimally, affected by these cookies. It's highly appreciated if you toggle the switch. Marketing & Social Media: If you want marketing campaigns and advertisements you see online and on social media to be tailored to your browsing behavior and the interests derived from it, you can enable the slider or click the 'Accept all' button. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time by making new choices in the menu. Click on 'Overview' at the top for a complete overview of the cookies in each category. Please see our cookies page for more information and to reset your cookie preferences. Functional Analytics Marketing & Social Media Reject all Accept Selection Accept all Eur.nl Functional Cookies and similar technologies that are strictly necessary for the website to work, such as remembering your preferences, security, enabling log-in or processing forms. Consent Studio Consent Studio consent-studio__consent-id ID of the proof of consent storage within the Consent Studio platform. 30 days consent-studio__storage Local storage for the consent given by the user for certain categories of cookies. 30 days consent-studio__seen Boolean that keeps track of whether the user has seen the cookie banner at least once. 30 days consent-studio__implicit-consent-triggered When a website has implicit consent configured, this cookie stores whether or not it has been triggered or not. 30 days consent-studio__gpc-consent-triggered Records that your browser's Global Privacy Control signal was detected, so non-essential cookies were automatically declined on your behalf. 30 days Cloudflare Cloudflare __cf_bm Helps Cloudflare tell people and automated programs apart, to protect the site from bots. 30 minutes _cfuvid Lets Cloudflare tell apart visitors who share the same internet connection, so traffic limits are applied fairly. Session cf_clearance Remembers that you passed a Cloudflare security check, so you are not asked again. 30 minutes HubSpot HubSpot hs_sessionid* Identifies your current visit so HubSpot can keep your session consistent while you browse. — Erasmus University Rotterdam CMS personalisation.segments This collects anonymous data about which category a visitor fits into. This allows us to offer the visitor content that matches their profile, based on visiting behaviour. — OnlineAfspraken.nl OnlineAfspraken.nl booking widget oa-dao-Resource* Stores the list of bookable resources, such as staff or rooms, that the appointment widget can offer. — oa-dao-ConsumerForm* Stores the layout and field definitions of the booking form, not the details you enter. — oa-dao-AppTypeGroup* Stores the categories used to group appointment types in the booking widget. — oa-booking Stores the details of the appointment you are currently booking. — oa-dao-* Stores appointment widget reference data on your device so the booking form does not have to reload it on every visit. — oa-application-widget-booking-consumerwidget-state Stores technical state the booking widget needs to work. — oa-dao-Mailing-MailingList-* Stores a mailing list that the appointment widget can offer you to subscribe to. — oa-configHash Stores a code used to check whether the booking widget has changed, so out-of-date saved booking data can be cleared. — oa-consumer Stores the identity of the signed-in customer for the booking. — oa-dao-AppType* Stores the list of appointment types the booking widget can offer. — oa-shoppingcart Stores the items you have added to your booking basket. — Analytics These cookies and similar technologies collect information about how visitors use our website, such as which pages are visited most, whether errors occur, and how users interact, to help us measure performance and improve the site. Google Google Analytics _ga ID used to identify users 2 years _ga_* Keeps track of your current visit for one specific Google Analytics property. 2 years eur.nl Website FPID Registers statistical data on users' behaviour on the website. Used for internal analytics by the website operator. — FPLC This FPLC cookie is the cross-domain linker cookie hashed from the FPID cookie. It’s not HttpOnly, which means it can be read with JavaScript. It has a relatively short lifetime, just 20 hours. — *__ga_* Keeps track of your current visit for one specific Google Analytics property. — *__ga Identifies your browser so Google Analytics can tell returning visitors from new ones. — *_FPID Identifies returning visitors so Google Analytics can report on visit patterns over time. 2 years *_FPLC Helps Google Analytics keep a consistent visitor identifier when you move between this site's subdomains or linked domains. 20 hours Hotjar Hotjar _hjSessionUser_* Stores a random ID that lets Hotjar recognise you when you return to the site. 1 year _hjSession_* Links the pages you view during one visit to the same Hotjar session. 30 minutes Marketing & Social Media These cookies and similar technologies help advertising and social media partners personalise your experience, show you relevant ads, measure campaign results, and enable sharing features. Google Google Ads _gcl_au Identifies your browser so Google can link a later purchase or sign-up on this site to the adverts you saw or clicked. 90 days IDE Recognises your browser so Google can measure how adverts perform and show you adverts that fit your interests. 13 months _gcl_ls This item is used by Google Ads to store advertising click identifiers for conversion measurement. When visitors do not accept tracking cookies, Google can send a cookieless ping via Consent Mode v2 with anonymized data to measure conversions and advertising performance. Data may be stored temporarily or persistently, depending on the implementation. — Google NID Lets Google remember your preferences and helps it choose which adverts to show you. 6 months __Secure-ENID Remembers your Google preferences, such as language, and can be used to choose which adverts you see. 13 months eur.nl Website FPAU Identifies your browser so Google can link a later purchase or sign-up on this site to the adverts you saw or clicked. 90 days *__fbp Stores a Meta (Facebook) browser identifier so visits and conversions can be attributed back to Meta advertising. — *__gcl_au Identifies your browser so Google can link a later purchase or sign-up on this site to the adverts you saw or clicked. 90 days *_FPAU Identifies your browser so Google can link a later purchase or sign-up on this site to the adverts you saw or clicked. 90 days LinkedIn LinkedIn lidc Helps LinkedIn choose which of its data centres handles your browser's requests. 1 day bcookie Identifies your browser to LinkedIn when LinkedIn content or advertising is loaded on this site. 1 year li_gc Remembers whether you agreed to LinkedIn's non-essential cookies as a visitor without a LinkedIn account. 6 months Meta Meta Pixel _fbp Identifies your browser to Meta, so your visits to this site can be used for advertising on Facebook and Instagram and to measure how adverts perform. 90 days lastExternalReferrer Detects how the user reached the website by registering their last URL-address — lastExternalReferrerTime Detects how the user reached the website by registering their last URL-address — Consent dialog opened"
    },
