    "https://www.eur.nl/en/working-at-eur/vacancies/internship-marketing-communications-1": {
      "title": "Internship Marketing & Communications",
      "description": "Internship Marketing & Communications | Working at | Erasmus University Rotterdam Skip to main content Skip to search Skip to subnavigation Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Close Open search Close Open menu Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Switch language to EN English current language NL Nederlands Search Close Search Search Primary Why work at EUR Open submenu Why work at EUR Campus Diversity Societal involvement Sustainability Working conditions Working areas Open submenu Working areas Academic staff Working in Finance Working in IT Working at Legal Affairs Working at Real Estate & Facilities PhD LDE traineeship International staff Practical information Open submenu Practical information Candidate portal Vacancies Internship Marketing & Communications Listen Published Friday 13 Nov 2026 Deadline Friday 27 Nov 2026 Work area Marketing & Communication Organisational unit Institute for Housing and Urban Development Studies (IHS) Employment 1 fte - 1 fte Introduction We are hiring a Marketing & Communications intern! Are you passionate about creating digital content? Do you enjoy connecting with students from around the world?  If so, we have the perfect opportunity for you! Join the IHS team as a Marketing & Communications Intern. We are looking for creative and proactive students pursuing a Bachelor’s degree in Marketing, Communication, International Business, or a related field, with a strong interest in cities and sustainability. Have a look at the vacancy below and submit your application by 27 November for the chance to join our team. Job description Internship Tasks & Responsibilities Create and publish various types of content for our online channels, including interviews, blog articles, videos, and podcasts. Assist with digital marketing by developing marketing materials and campaigns, such as ad copy and email content. Help track, report, and analyse the performance of marketing campaigns. Support the organisation of both offline and online events. Facilitate communication with external stakeholders, such as prospective students, alumni, and partners. Assist in managing our CRM system, including data entry and email marketing. Support student communication and contribute to improving day-to-day office operations Provide assistance with general and ad-hoc departmental activities. Job requirements To be eligible, you must be enrolled as a student at a Dutch or foreign university and have a residence permit for the Netherlands if you are not an EU citizen. You should be pursuing a graduate or undergraduate programme (Master's or Bachelor's) that includes a mandatory work placement or internship with an international organisation, such as IHS. Furthermore, we are looking for candidates who demonstrate the following qualities: A creative and proactive attitude when working in teams, along with the ability to work independently. The capability to manage multiple tasks simultaneously while meeting deadlines. International work experience in a multicultural environment is advantageous. An excellent command of both written and spoken English. Strong organisational skills. Proficiency in computer skills, particularly with Microsoft Office. Specific Skills Candidates must have successfully completed at least two years of an undergraduate degree in one of the following disciplines: International Business, Communication, Marketing, or a related field.  Any relevant work experience in these areas will be considered an asset. Candidates should have a strong affinity for marketing and communication, as well as an interest in urban sustainability and visual communication/design. Knowledge, experience, and interest in the following topics will be advantageous: Communication and marketing concepts Basic marketing theory Digital and online tools Research and analysis Additionally, strong writing skills are essential. Familiarity with Canva and basic video editing skills will be appreciated and will be taken into account during the selection process. Employment conditions and benefits What we offer A compensation of 500 euros gross per month regardless of educational level per 1 January 2027. A compensation for your travel costs to/from work (for a distance of up to 15 km) An international work environment Convenient location on the Woudestein Campus (access to sports facilities, restaurants and more) Possibility to take ownership of your own projects and develop soft skills such as goal setting, teamwork, and time management Training on our latest CRM, project management and CMS Personalised mentorship and career learning development tracking Free coffee and tea, along with occasional snacks Fun social events with our master’s students and staff such as intercultural evenings and karaoke nights Terms & Conditions IHS will establish an internship agreement that states the terms and conditions of the internship. This document needs to be signed by IHS, a representative of the intern’s university and the intern. Candidates that cannot provide university approval for the respective agreement cannot be accepted. The candidate must have a Dutch residence permit valid for the total period of the internship or be an EU citizen . Candidates without a permit cannot be accepted.  The intern position is available in Rotterdam, the Netherlands, for up to six months (preferred duration) and needs a presence of 40 hrs per week, working regular office hours. The duration of this internship will be from 1 February 2027 until July or August 2027 . Concrete dates to be discussed depending on the available starting date of the candidate and the availability of the internship at that particular time. Faculty / Institute / Central service The Institute for Housing and Urban Development Studies (IHS) is a centre of urban expertise at Erasmus University Rotterdam. At IHS, we envision liveable, socially, economically, and environmentally sustainable cities. Our mission is to inspire and empower urban professionals and citizens to make cities work for all. Looking at cities from different perspectives, we educate urban professionals from diverse backgrounds, provide consultancy services to national and local governments and engage in cutting-edge urban research. Bringing practical experience from real-life projects back to the classroom, we inspire collaboration and co-creation of urban knowledge. Together with our partners, we work at the forefront of urban development to improve the wellbeing of people living in cities across the globe. IHS has approximately 55 staff– while we are based in Rotterdam, we have a strong interdisciplinary and international outlook and approach. The Institute for Housing and Urban Development Studies (IHS) is a research, advisory, and education institute that operates under the Erasmus School of Social and Behavioural Sciences (ESSB) and the Erasmus School of Economics (ESE). IHS is part of the EUR Holding BV. Additional information For more information about IHS, please visit our website www.ihs.nl . Applying The application procedure consists of 1 interview and 1 assignment. You can apply for this position up to and including 27 November. Attach your cover letter and CV to your application in English. We look forward to receiving your application. IHS offers equal opportunities to all employees and applicants, regardless of gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, ethnicity, age, neurodiversity, disability, citizenship or any other aspect that makes them unique. We hope to welcome you in our community. Stay up to date with new vacancies! Want to be the first to know about vacancies that match your interests? Let us know what you're looking for, and we'll send you an email as soon as a new opportunity that fits your profile is posted.\nDon’t miss out on your perfect job! Sign up Close Stay up to date with new vacancies! Share this page Interested? Applicant portal Open navigation for Internship Marketing & Communications Close Interested? Interested? Compare 0 study programme Close Compare 0 study programme Compare study programmes Breadcrumb Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Vacancies Internship Marketing & Communications Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Directly to Information Directly to Why work at EUR Working areas International staff Practical information Vacancies Information ANBI Cookies Disclaimer Privacy statement Accessibility Our channels Facebook Instagram X (formerly twitter) Linkedin Youtube Making Minds Matter Watch the video Close"
    },
